### What is association vs aggregation vs composition?

Three levels of coupling from weakest to strongest.

### What does each relationship look like in code?

```java
// Association: TradeService uses MarketDataProvider
public class TradeService {
    private final MarketDataProvider marketData; // uses
    public TradeService(MarketDataProvider marketData) { this.marketData = marketData; }
}
// Neither owns the other. Both independent. Injected via Spring.

// Aggregation: Portfolio has Stocks
public class Portfolio {
    private final java.util.List<Stock> stocks = new java.util.ArrayList<>();
    public void addStock(Stock stock) { stocks.add(stock); } // created outside
    public java.util.List<Stock> liquidate() {
        var released = new java.util.ArrayList<>(stocks);
        stocks.clear();
        return released; // stocks survive
    }
}

// Composition: TradeOrder owns OrderLines
public class TradeOrder {
    private final String orderId;
    private final java.util.List<OrderLine> lines = new java.util.ArrayList<>();
    public void addLine(String symbol, int qty, java.math.BigDecimal price) {
        lines.add(new OrderLine(orderId + "-L" + (lines.size() + 1), symbol, qty, price));
        // Order creates order lines
    }
    public void cancel() { lines.clear(); } // lines destroyed with order
}
```

### What is the UML notation?

```text
Association:    TradeService ────────→ MarketDataProvider
                (plain line with arrow: uses)

Aggregation:    Portfolio ◇─────────→ Stock
                (hollow diamond: has, part survives)

Composition:    TradeOrder ◆─────────→ OrderLine
                (filled diamond: owns, part dies with whole)

Diamond is on the PARENT side (the whole).
```

### How do all three compare?

| Aspect | Association | Aggregation | Composition |
|--------|------------|-------------|-------------|
| Relationship | Uses-A | Has-A (weak) | Owns-A (strong) |
| Lifecycle | Independent | Independent | Bound |
| Child survives? | Yes | Yes | No |
| UML | Arrow | Hollow diamond | Filled diamond |
| JPA cascade | None | None | cascade ALL |
| Example | Service uses Provider | Portfolio has Stocks | Order owns Lines |

### What is the decision rule?

Can the part exist meaningfully without the whole? Yes and no ownership -> association. Yes but contained -> aggregation. No -> composition.

### What should a senior engineer know?

- In Domain-Driven Design, composition maps to entities within an Aggregate Root.
- In event-driven architecture, associations are cross-service references, aggregation is within-service collections, and composition is within-aggregate ownership.
